data.content:
The `SafeAreaEdges="None"` on the page only tells the page layout not to add safe-area padding, but the content itself still respects the safe area boundaries by default. You likely need two additional things:

**1. Set `IgnoreSafeArea` on the Image (or its parent layout):**

```xml
<Image Source="photo.jpg"
       Aspect="AspectFill"
       IgnoreSafeArea="True" />
```

**2. Enable edge-to-edge rendering (Android):**

In .NET 10 (and enforced on Android 15+), you need to explicitly opt into edge-to-edge. In your `MainActivity.cs` or platform code:

```csharp
#if ANDROID
using AndroidX.Activity;

// In your MainActivity or App lifecycle:
EdgeToEdge.Enable(Platform.CurrentActivity as ComponentActivity);
#endif
```

Or in your `MauiProgram.cs` using the lifecycle events:

```csharp
builder.ConfigureLifecycleEvents(events =>
{
    events.AddAndroid(android => android.OnCreate((activity, _) =>
    {
        EdgeToEdge.Enable(activity);
    }));
});
```

**Summary:** `SafeAreaEdges="None"` prevents the *page* from adding padding, but `IgnoreSafeArea="True"` on the view is what actually lets content draw behind the system bars. On Android, you also need edge-to-edge mode enabled for the window to extend under the status/navigation bars.
